<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Page-1" id="-yTnNuizEo4m1ANID7nL">
    <mxGraphModel dx="2946" dy="1690" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="827" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <UserObject label="" mermaidData="{&#xa;  &quot;data&quot;: &quot;classDiagram\n  class User {\n    -int userId\n    -String name\n    -String email\n    -Role role\n    +getRole() Role\n    +requestToken() Token\n    +cancelToken() void\n  }\n\n  class Token {\n    -int tokenId\n    -String tokenNumber\n    -TokenStatus status\n    -DateTime issueTime\n    -DateTime callTime\n    -DateTime completionTime\n    +calculateWaitingTime() int\n    +calculateServiceTime() int\n    +cancel() void\n  }\n\n  class Counter {\n    -int counterId\n    -String counterNumber\n    -boolean available\n    +callToken(Token token) void\n    +completeToken(Token token) void\n    +getWorkload() int\n  }\n\n  class QueueManager {\n    -int queueId\n    -int averageWaitingTime\n    +issueToken(User user) Token\n    +assignToken(Token token, Counter counter) void\n    +updateDashboard() void\n  }\n\n  class ServiceRequest {\n    -int requestId\n    -String serviceType\n    -String status\n    -Decimal amount\n    +submit() void\n    +approve() void\n    +reject() void\n  }\n\n  class Receipt {\n    -int receiptId\n    -DateTime issuedAt\n    -String details\n    +generate() void\n  }\n\n  class AlertService {\n    -int alertId\n    -String alertType\n    -String message\n    +checkQueueLength() Alert\n    +checkWaitingTime() Alert\n    +sendAlert(Alert alert) void\n  }\n\n  class Alert {\n    -int alertId\n    -String alertType\n    -String message\n    -DateTime createdAt\n    +markAsRead() void\n  }\n\n  class ReportService {\n    -String reportType\n    -Date startDate\n    -Date endDate\n    +generateReport() String\n    +getHistoricalData() String\n  }\n\n  class AuditLog {\n    -int logId\n    -DateTime timestamp\n    -String action\n    -String details\n    +recordAction() void\n  }\n\n  enum Role {\n    USER\n    ADMINISTRATOR\n    MANAGER\n  }\n\n  enum TokenStatus {\n    WAITING\n    CALLED\n    IN_SERVICE\n    COMPLETED\n    CANCELLED\n  }\n\n  User \&quot;1\&quot; --&gt; \&quot;0..*\&quot; Token : requests\n  User \&quot;1\&quot; --&gt; \&quot;0..*\&quot; ServiceRequest : submits\n  User \&quot;1\&quot; --&gt; \&quot;0..*\&quot; AuditLog : creates\n  User \&quot;1\&quot; --&gt; \&quot;0..1\&quot; Alert : receives\n\n  QueueManager \&quot;1\&quot; o-- \&quot;0..*\&quot; Token : manages\n  QueueManager \&quot;1\&quot; --&gt; \&quot;1..*\&quot; Counter : coordinates\n  Counter \&quot;1\&quot; --&gt; \&quot;0..*\&quot; Token : serves\n  Token \&quot;1\&quot; --&gt; \&quot;0..*\&quot; ServiceRequest : contains\n  ServiceRequest \&quot;1\&quot; --&gt; \&quot;0..1\&quot; Receipt : produces\n\n  AlertService \&quot;1\&quot; --&gt; \&quot;0..*\&quot; Alert : creates\n  AlertService ..&gt; QueueManager : monitors\n  AlertService ..&gt; Token : checks waiting time\n  ReportService ..&gt; Token : analyzes\n  ReportService ..&gt; Counter : analyzes workload\n  ReportService ..&gt; ServiceRequest : analyzes\n  ReportService ..&gt; AuditLog : reads\n\n  AuditLog ..&gt; Token : records token actions\n  AuditLog ..&gt; ServiceRequest : records request actions\n  AuditLog ..&gt; Counter : records counter actions\n\n  User ..&gt; Role : uses\n  Token ..&gt; TokenStatus : uses\n\nA. Class purposes\n\n- `User`: Stores user identity and role information.\n- `Token`: Represents a customer’s queue position and timing.\n- `Counter`: Represents a bank service counter.\n- `QueueManager`: Issues tokens and manages the queue.\n- `ServiceRequest`: Represents one requested banking service.\n- `Receipt`: Represents proof of a completed service.\n- `AlertService`: Detects queue and waiting-time problems.\n- `Alert`: Stores an alert shown to a manager.\n- `ReportService`: Produces historical and workload reports.\n- `AuditLog`: Records important system actions.\n- `Role`: Defines the three allowed user roles.\n- `TokenStatus`: Defines the token life cycle.\n\nB. Relationship table\n\n| Class A | Class B | Type | Multiplicity | Why it exists |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| User | Token | Association | `1` to `0..*` | A user may request many tokens. |\n| User | ServiceRequest | Association | `1` to `0..*` | A user may submit many service requests. |\n| User | AuditLog | Association | `1` to `0..*` | User actions can be recorded. |\n| User | Alert | Association | `1` to `0..1` | A user may receive an alert. |\n| QueueManager | Token | Aggregation | `1` to `0..*` | The queue manager manages tokens, but tokens can exist independently. |\n| QueueManager | Counter | Association | `1` to `1..*` | The queue manager coordinates one or more counters. |\n| Counter | Token | Association | `1` to `0..*` | A counter can serve many tokens over time. |\n| Token | ServiceRequest | Association | `1` to `0..*` | A token may contain one or more requested services. |\n| ServiceRequest | Receipt | Association | `1` to `0..1` | A completed request may produce one receipt. |\n| AlertService | Alert | Association | `1` to `0..*` | The service creates alerts. |\n| AlertService | QueueManager | Dependency | no fixed ownership | It checks queue conditions. |\n| AlertService | Token | Dependency | no fixed ownership | It checks waiting times. |\n| ReportService | Token | Dependency | no fixed ownership | It analyzes token data. |\n| ReportService | Counter | Dependency | no fixed ownership | It analyzes counter workload. |\n| ReportService | ServiceRequest | Dependency | no fixed ownership | It analyzes service records. |\n| ReportService | AuditLog | Dependency | no fixed ownership | It reads audit history for reports. |\n| AuditLog | Token | Dependency | no fixed ownership | It records token actions. |\n| AuditLog | ServiceRequest | Dependency | no fixed ownership | It records service actions. |\n| AuditLog | Counter | Dependency | no fixed ownership | It records counter actions. |\n| User | Role | Enum usage | one role per user | The role controls access rights. |\n| Token | TokenStatus | Enum usage | one status per token | The enum controls the token life cycle. |\n\nC. Role usage\n\n- `USER`\n  - Uses `User` to identify the customer.\n  - Uses `QueueManager` to request a token.\n  - Uses `Token` to check waiting time or cancel.\n  - Uses `ServiceRequest` to submit a banking service.\n  - May receive `Alert`.\n  - Receives `Receipt` after completion.\n\n- `ADMINISTRATOR`\n  - Uses `QueueManager` to receive and call tokens.\n  - Uses `Counter` to process customers.\n  - Uses `ServiceRequest` to approve or reject requests.\n  - Uses `Receipt` to provide proof of service.\n  - Creates `AuditLog` records through system actions.\n  - Manages users and counters through the application services.\n\n- `MANAGER`\n  - Uses `AlertService` for long-queue and excessive-wait alerts.\n  - Uses `ReportService` for historical reports.\n  - Reads `AuditLog` records.\n  - Monitors `QueueManager`, `Token`, `Counter`, and `ServiceRequest` data through the dashboard.\n\nD. Customer journey\n\n1. The `User` asks `QueueManager` for a token.\n2. `QueueManager` creates a `Token` with status `WAITING`.\n3. The `QueueManager` assigns the token to a `Counter`.\n4. The `Counter` calls the token and changes its status to `CALLED`.\n5. The `User` submits a `ServiceRequest`.\n6. The administrator processes the request.\n7. The administrator approves or rejects it using `ServiceRequest`.\n8. The `Counter` completes the token.\n9. The `Token` stores waiting and service times.\n10. A `Receipt` is generated for the completed request.\n11. The action is recorded in `AuditLog`.\n\nE. Likely instructor questions\n\n1. Why is there only one `ServiceRequest` class?  \n   Different banking services share the same workflow. The `serviceType` field identifies account opening, deposits, withdrawals, bill payments, or fund transfers.\n\n2. Why is `Role` an enum?  \n   The system has exactly three roles. An enum prevents invalid role values.\n\n3. Why does `Token` use `TokenStatus`?  \n   The status clearly shows the token life cycle, such as waiting, called, completed, or cancelled.\n\n4. Why is the relationship between `QueueManager` and `Token` aggregation?  \n   The queue manager organizes tokens, but a token is still a separate object. It can be stored, audited, or reported independently.\n\n5. Why are `AlertService` and `ReportService` dependencies instead of inheritance?  \n   They use data from other classes but do not represent specialized versions of those classes. Dependency is the simpler and more accurate relationship.\n\nF. Verification checklist\n\n- Class names use PascalCase.\n- Member names use camelCase.\n- Private attributes use `-`.\n- Public methods use `+`.\n- Only the required core classes and enums are included.\n- `ServiceRequest` is a single class with `serviceType`.\n- No unnecessary inheritance is used.\n- Relationships show meaningful multiplicities.\n- `Role` contains exactly three roles.\n- `TokenStatus` represents the token life cycle.\n- Queue management, waiting time, service time, workload, alerts, reports, audit logging, and receipts are covered.\n- All classes are connected and used.\n- The classes match the three roles in the use case diagram.&quot;,&#xa;  &quot;config&quot;: null,&#xa;  &quot;version&quot;: &quot;12&quot;&#xa;}" id="eLky1msA_2WelXA9fJMR-1">
          <mxCell connectable="0" parent="1" style="group;transparentBounds=1;editIcon=1;lockedGroup=0;groupPadding=10;labelBackgroundColor=none;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
